docs/analytics/posthog-operating-plan.md:1:# PostHog product analytics operating plan
docs/analytics/posthog-operating-plan.md:3:This is the source of truth for Keating's web analytics. It turns product behavior into a small set of questions that can be answered repeatedly, while keeping learner and model-authored content out of PostHog.
docs/analytics/posthog-operating-plan.md:21:- Dynamic route IDs, query strings, and URL fragments are removed in `web/src/lib/analytics-privacy.ts`.
docs/analytics/posthog-operating-plan.md:24:- The app remains fully functional after analytics opt-out or when a blocker prevents PostHog from loading.
docs/analytics/posthog-operating-plan.md:29:The PostHog client registers these on every event:
docs/analytics/posthog-operating-plan.md:33:| `analytics_schema_version` | Event contract version. Increment for breaking semantic changes. |
docs/analytics/posthog-operating-plan.md:47:| `$pageview` | PostHog history-change page view | Sanitized route and referrer |
docs/analytics/posthog-operating-plan.md:57:One user-visible run can contain multiple provider generations when tools are used. Product lifecycle events describe the whole run; PostHog `$ai_generation` events describe each provider call.
docs/analytics/posthog-operating-plan.md:62:| `$ai_generation` | Each provider `turn_end` | `$ai_trace_id`, `$ai_span_id`, `$ai_model`, `$ai_provider`, `$ai_latency`, `$ai_time_to_first_token`, `$ai_is_error`, `$ai_stop_reason`; token counts when available |
docs/analytics/posthog-operating-plan.md:66:Do not set `$ai_input` or `$ai_output_choices`. Content-free traces still support latency, errors, cost/token trends, tool overhead, and model comparisons.
docs/analytics/posthog-operating-plan.md:129:Create these in PostHog so targeting, sampling, and copy can change without a deployment. Use one survey per purpose and keep free text optional.
docs/analytics/posthog-operating-plan.md:154:Use PostHog experiment exposure events and decide the sample size and minimum runtime before launch. Do not ship permanent forks guarded by stale flags. Record the decision and remove the losing branch.
docs/analytics/posthog-operating-plan.md:156:## PostHog project setup
docs/analytics/posthog-operating-plan.md:162:5. Configure exception tracking and upload production source maps with the Vite plugin. The build must stay valid when PostHog secrets are absent, and source maps must not remain in public assets after upload.
docs/analytics/posthog-operating-plan.md:164:7. Validate in PostHog Live Events with a synthetic session: landing CTA, composer, first message, successful turn, model change, auth failure/recovery, tool use, quiz, share, and opt-out.
docs/analytics/posthog-operating-plan.md:171:| `VITE_POSTHOG_PROJECT_TOKEN` | Public project ingest token. Analytics is inert when absent. |
docs/analytics/posthog-operating-plan.md:172:| `VITE_POSTHOG_HOST` | PostHog UI host. Browser ingest remains same-origin through `/ingest`. |
docs/analytics/posthog-operating-plan.md:173:| `VITE_POSTHOG_DISABLED` | Emergency client analytics kill switch. |
docs/analytics/posthog-operating-plan.md:174:| `VITE_POSTHOG_SESSION_REPLAY` | Explicit build-time replay allow switch. Defaults off in Docker. |
docs/analytics/posthog-operating-plan.md:175:| `POSTHOG_API_KEY` | Secret personal API key used only by the production build to upload source maps. |
docs/analytics/posthog-operating-plan.md:176:| `POSTHOG_PROJECT_ID` | Project receiving source maps. |
docs/analytics/posthog-operating-plan.md:180:## Definition of done for analytics changes
docs/analytics/posthog-operating-plan.md:184:- The event is verified in a real browser and, when credentials are available, in PostHog Live Events.
docs/analytics/posthog-operating-plan.md:185:- Funnel step names remain stable or the analytics schema version changes.
docs/analytics/posthog-operating-plan.md:186:- Product behavior still works with PostHog blocked and after user opt-out.
